@startuml seq-15-websocket-notifications
title WebSocket Notifications — Real-Time Push (native WS, JWT query param)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
autonumber

actor "Authenticated\nUser (Angular)" as User
participant "Gateway\n:9000\n(lb:ws://)" as GW
participant "Messaging\nService :9007\n(TextWebSocket\nHandler)" as MSG
participant "WsSessions\nMap<user,sessions>" as Sessions
participant "Other User\n(Sender)" as Sender

note over User : EventSource cannot send Authorization header\nWebSocket uses ?token=JWT query param instead (ADR-14)

== WebSocket connection establishment ==

User -> GW : WS Upgrade GET /ws/notifications?token=<JWT>
note right of GW : /ws/** is permitAll at gateway\nMessaging-service validates JWT itself
GW -> MSG : proxy WS upgrade (lb:ws://messaging-service)
MSG -> MSG : JwtDecoder.decode(token)\nextract username from JWT sub
MSG -> Sessions : register session for username
Sessions --> MSG : session stored
MSG --> User : 101 Switching Protocols (WS established)

== Sender sends a message ==

Sender -> GW : POST /api/messages/send\nBearer JWT\n{ recipientId:"analyst-user", content:"Alert update" }
GW -> MSG : lb://messaging-service
MSG -> MSG : persist message to Postgres\n(messaging_db)
MSG -> Sessions : get sessions for "analyst-user"
Sessions --> MSG : WebSocketSession(s)

MSG -> User : WS TEXT frame\n{ type:"NEW_MESSAGE", fromUser:"admin-user",\n  unreadCount:3, timestamp }
User -> User : FAB badge updates to "3"\nrouter: navigate to /messages

== Unread count on app load ==

User -> GW : GET /api/messages/unread-count\nBearer JWT
GW -> MSG : route
MSG -> MSG : count unread in Postgres\nwhere recipient=username AND readAt IS NULL
MSG --> User : 200 { count: 3 }

== Mark thread as read ==

User -> GW : POST /api/messages/mark-read/{peerId}\nBearer JWT
GW -> MSG : route
MSG -> MSG : UPDATE messages SET readAt=now\nWHERE recipient=username AND sender=peerId
MSG --> User : 200 OK
MSG -> Sessions : notify sender of read receipt (optional)

@enduml
